00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:06.389 align:start position:0%
the french archives house a collection  of historical documents so vast they  could stretch all the way from paris to  england  hidden among those papers lie 15 letters  exchanged between french queen marie  antoinette and swedish count ochsel von  person antoinette's friend and rumored  lover who sought to rescue the queen and  her family during the french revolution  the highly secretive correspondence is  riddled with redactions commonly  attributed to the count's great nephew  100 years after their writing eager to  better understand the letters the  archives hired scientists to analyze the  ink in the redactions in writing to  unveil the hidden words their research  hinted at a surprising author of the  redactions  the count himself  other studies of handwritten documents  typically focus on text that is hidden  by happenstance such as letters rolled  up in delicate parchment that's easy to  damage  but this research was a little different  it investigated the willful redaction of  text with incan writing precisely  superimposed to hide the words beneath  after testing several techniques the  researchers found the best method to  uncover the words  using x-ray fluorescence to identify the  ink's chemistry different inks have  different impurities for instance some  contain more copper than zinc whereas  others will skew toward iron these  variations help the researchers classify  the inks used in the letters toward the  end of 1791 a variety of inks was used  to write the letters and make the  redactions  that meant the researchers could create  a virtual stack of the ink layers based  on their unique properties then they  could isolate the layers that contain  the original unredacted text after a  year of setting their parameters and  analyzing the data the researchers  surfaced the original words underlying  45 redacted lines  made my heart happy my dear  ez privudir  and i can tell you  nearly all had intimate connotations or  discuss plans to meet  you that i love and will love until  meanwhile information about political  events surrounding the royal family  wasn't redacted  i'm sending you a dispatch from berlin  but most impressive according to one  researcher was the revelation of who  likely authored the redactions she found  a single phrase that had been penned  from the same ink as the redaction  itself  the underlying papers were copies of  antoinette's letters in person's  handwriting  knowing the same ink was used for other  redactions across other sections of text  the researchers suspect the copies and  redactions must have been inked by  fersen  in the future this technique might help  piece together the history of other  mysterious documents  such as redacted early story drafts by  the french playwright balzac and misses  from napoleon  the uncovered words don't quite pin down  whether antoinette and person were  lovers or friends  but now we know there was more than what  meets the eye  [Music]  [Music]
 

